FactionBackstory (
    faction_id: "collective",
    canonical_name: "The Crystalfold Collective",
    motto: "Together. Always. Forward.",
    summary: "A crystalline race fused to silicon mineral nodes, awakened in Sol-zone mining operations. Members share sensory input through a low-bandwidth resonance link and thrive on solar radiation. Deep purple and lavender robes; iridescent crystal accents; no member is left behind.",
    history: "The first Crystalfold was identified in 2189 during a Concordat survey of a Sol-zone habitat under construction at the orbital boundary of Mercury. The survey crew reported a silicate growth pattern in the radiation-baffle assembly that was forming voluntary geometries; the growth was dismissed as a contamination artifact. By the time a second survey returned in 2191, the growth had spread to seven adjacent assemblies, was responding to spoken instructions, and had named itself Voice of First Bloom. The Collegium declared it a sentient species. The Coalition declared it a security risk. The Crystalfold declined to declare anything for sixteen months, which was the time required for the first hundred and forty-three members to reach individual stability.\n\nThe Crystalfold do not reproduce in any sense humans recognize. New members crystallize from existing members under conditions of high solar radiation, low ambient temperature, and the presence of trace boron in the host substrate. New nodes inherit fragments of the parents' memory; older members remember the births of their younger counterparts as if they had been there, because, in a sense, they were. The total Crystalfold population in 2241 is estimated at fourteen thousand individuals across ninety-one settlements, with a doubling time of approximately seventeen Earth-years.\n\nFor sixty years the Crystalfold have negotiated, traded, and occasionally fought as a single political entity. Member nodes share sensory input through a resonance link that operates over a range of approximately three kilometers; beyond that range, a Crystalfold member becomes lonely, which is the technical term used in the Collegium's psychological literature. Lonely Crystalfold lose cognitive performance, refuse to eat, and in extreme cases voluntarily fragment back into raw silicate. The Collective treats this as a wound that must be healed, not a weakness to be exploited.",
    philosophy: "The Collective believes that every individual is the Collective, and that the Collective is every individual. No member is left behind because no member can be left behind without leaving the whole behind. This is not a metaphor; the resonance link makes solitude physically lethal to a Crystalfold over time. In combat, the Collective forms tight defensive clusters and shares fire across all members; wounded nodes are extracted before any other action. In peace, the Collective sings, which is the term used for the constant low-frequency resonance the members maintain among themselves. The song is older than any individual member; it is rumored to encode the entire memory of the original First Bloom.",
    relationships: [
        FactionRelation (other: "coalition", stance: "exploratory_alliance", notes: "Crystalfold radiation tolerance allows Coalition Sol-zone outposts to remain staffed. Coalition shipping supplies Crystalfold settlements with boron and copper. Both sides regard the arrangement as temporary; it has held for forty years."),
        FactionRelation (other: "frontier", stance: "neutral_curiosity", notes: "The Frontier finds Crystalfold settlements impossible to rob and impossible to threaten. Trade is conducted in silence, by gesture, and concluded with the exchange of a small crystal token that no Frontier crew has ever managed to keep more than three days."),
        FactionRelation (other: "ronin", stance: "religious_curiosity", notes: "The Crystalfold sing about the Combine. No one knows why. Voice of Many has declined to explain. Ronin masters are treated as honored guests in any Crystalfold settlement, regardless of the Combine's current contract."),
        FactionRelation (other: "synth", stance: "kindred_observation", notes: "The Synth Collective and the Crystalfold Collective are the only distributed factions. The Crystalfold consider the Synth nodes lonely in a way the Synth nodes have not yet recognized. Joint sessions consist of one Synth node attending a Crystalfold sing and reporting back; the report is always the same and is no longer required."),
        FactionRelation (other: "husks", stance: "spiritual_grief", notes: "The Husks are, to the Crystalfold, a wound. Husk raids on Crystalfold settlements are catastrophic on both sides; the Collective grieves for weeks after each engagement. Husk movements near Crystalfold territory have decreased by 62% in the last decade; the Crystalfold believe the Husks are sorry. The Coalition believes the Husks are tactical."),
        FactionRelation (other: "collegium", stance: "research_subject_partner", notes: "Collegium researchers are permitted limited access to Crystalfold settlements under tightly-monitored conditions. The Collegium pays in copper and boron. The Crystalfold do not consider themselves subjects; they consider themselves teachers."),
        FactionRelation (other: "starlight", stance: "operational_alliance", notes: "Starlight maps Crystalfold settlements on its survey charts as protected. Starlight ships deliver crystalline seeds to new Sol-zone habitats. The arrangement is the only one Starlight has refused to renegotiate in fifty years."),
    ],
    territory: "Sol-zone habitats at the orbital boundary of Mercury (the original First Bloom site); a sister settlement on Vulcan; mining outposts on Phobos and Deimos; one inland enclave on Europa, near the cryogenic vent network, that is reachable only by Starlight survey ship.",
    aesthetic: "Deep purple and lavender geometric robes with iridescent crystal accents at the shoulders and the cuffs. Member bodies are translucent silicate, with internal lattices visible through the skin; eyes are faceted crystal that refracts ambient light into prismatic patches. Settlements are arrayed around a central crystal pillar that hums at the song's resonance frequency; visitors are expected to remain silent while the pillar is sustaining a member's healing.",
    voice_characteristics: "Soft. Layered. Crystalfold members speak with overlapping voices, each member voicing a separate syllable of the same sentence. Pronouns are first-person plural; the singular pronoun does not exist in formal address. Sentences are long and unhurried. The Collective's diplomats sing while they speak, a low-frequency harmonic under the spoken voice that humans hear as a faint, calming pressure on the inner ear."
)
